libva-v4l2-request (1.2+opi5.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 10-bit HEVC/VP9 keep their depth: 10-bit configs offer P010 surfaces
    (exported as DRM_FORMAT_P010) and the decoder's packed NV15 is
    converted to P010 instead of truncated to NV12. The conversion runs on
    a V4L2 mem2mem converter that can do it (RK3588 RGA3 with NV15 input),
    else on the CPU (NEON, 4 threads) when the frame is first read.
  * Keep every mem2mem converter found, not only the first one: on the
    RK3588 the first is the RGA2, which cannot read NV15.
  * With the CPU route, HEVC Main10 and VP9 Profile 2 are now also offered
    on kernels whose RGA cannot read NV15 (V4L2R_NO_CPU_CONVERT=1 turns
    this off).
  * NV12 output for 8-bit streams is unchanged.
  * vaprobe lists the surface formats of each decode config.

 -- Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 01:10:00 +0000

libva-v4l2-request (1.2+opi5.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Reset pooled decoder descriptors with the device's own queue types: the
    reset stopped all four buffer types, and the failing STREAMOFF of the
    two the device lacks left the kernel context aborted, so a later decode
    context on the descriptor never ran a job (Firefox 4K and 10-bit AV1).
  * AV1: derive the tile sizes of uniform tile spacing instead of taking
    VA's width/height_in_sbs_minus_1, which Chromium leaves zero then; the
    VPU981 timed out on every frame (Chrome AV1 at ~1.4 frames/s).
  * Log when readers of an exported buffer hold up a decode.

 -- Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0000

libva-v4l2-request (1.2+opi5.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * AV1: accept the slice data buffer ahead of its slice parameters
    (Chromium's order), so Chrome decodes AV1 in hardware instead of
    failing the first vaEndPicture and falling back to dav1d.
  * AV1: take the CAPTURE bit depth from the sequence, so 10-bit streams
    decode to P010 (matching the client's surfaces), not down-converted NV12.
  * Restart decode waits interrupted by signals, and log the kernel's buffer
    state when a wait times out.

 -- Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0000

libva-v4l2-request (1.2+opi5.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Advertise HEVC Main10 / VP9 Profile 2 only when the format converter
    reads the decoder's 10-bit format (NV15); the mainline RGA does not, so
    the profiles were listed and then failed on the first frame.
  * AV1: let the sequence pick the CAPTURE bit depth, so 10-bit AV1 decodes
    to P010 through the VPU981 post-processor instead of being refused.

 -- Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0000

libva-v4l2-request (1.2+opi5.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix a deadlock in vaQueryConfigProfiles() (converter probe took the
    driver mutex already held by the caller); add tests/locking_test.

